.sessions-worktree/

# The doc gates are the only Node code in this repo, and js-yaml is their only
# dependency. Nothing needed ignoring here until the v6 gates arrived.
node_modules/

# `settings-policy.mjs --write` drops a timestamped backup beside the file it edits.
# Nothing ignored them in seeds, so every write left another one staged for commit.
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Env / secrets — everything matching .env* is a secret, no exceptions (DEC-S043).
# The template, if this repo ever needs one, is `env.example` — outside the namespace,
# so there is no negation to keep in sync.
.env*

# The offline firmware-signing key (DEC-013). It belongs OUTSIDE this checkout entirely —
# ~/.soundings/ota-signing-key is what the tooling suggests — and this rule is a seatbelt
# for the day someone drops a copy here "just while testing".
#
# ⚠ Worse than a leaked WiFi password, which is the precedent that earned firmware/'s
# *secret*.ini rule. A rotated password costs a USB trip per node; a leaked SIGNING key
# lets anyone publish firmware every node in the fleet will accept and execute, and the
# fix is a new key flashed over USB to every node — the exact cost the whole task exists
# to avoid. Nothing detects the leak in between.
#
# Deliberately NOT named `.env*`: that namespace is a blanket permission deny fleet-wide
# (DEC-S043), so a secret living there is one no session can read in order to debug it.
*ota-signing-key*

# Per-machine, never shared — the output style and any local permission overrides.
.claude/settings.local.json
